WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.758 --> 00:00:03.686
LETITIA WRIGHT
The detail. The colors.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:07.986
The beauty, the integrity.
Absolute integrity with Ruth Carter.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:12.484
RUTH E. CARTER
Wakanda itself is such a concept.

00:00:12.535 --> 00:00:16.473
We really wanted to come back to it.
This film gives you more.

00:00:16.523 --> 00:00:21.114
More military, landscapes, cultures,
technology that's upgraded.

00:00:21.164 --> 00:00:22.940
And much more M'Baku.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.440
[M'Baku yelling]

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.435
RYAN COOGLER
Ruth Carter really just took that initiative

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:29.903
and pushed the film farther than I could
ever imagine. I just kind of keep my eyes

00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:32.698
and ears open to the
brilliance of her bringing it to life.

00:00:32.749 --> 00:00:35.294
RUTH E. CARTER
We want to present the Wakanda that

00:00:35.344 --> 00:00:40.016
people know, and the Dora Milaje were
a big part of that Wakandan culture.

00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:43.961
We also wanted to upgrade
their armor and give them

00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:48.939
the ability to swim in that costume.
So, we had to create the new Dora Milaje.

00:00:49.023 --> 00:00:51.906
ANGELA BASSETT
Ruth is giving us PhD, graduate,

00:00:51.956 --> 00:00:57.356
beyond, beyond level. The embroidery,
the jewelry, the capes, the headdress.

00:00:57.407 --> 00:00:58.616
She just took it up a notch.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:01.665
QUEEN RAMONDA
Everyone seems to be working diligently.

00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:04.893
ANGELA BASSETT
Ruth will exhaust every possibility,

00:01:04.943 --> 00:01:09.455
in terms of her research,
to build this world of Wakanda.

00:01:09.505 --> 00:01:13.320
And not just Wakanda this time,
now the Talokan.

00:01:14.102 --> 00:01:17.445
NAMOR
My people call me K'uk'ulkan,

00:01:18.648 --> 00:01:20.224
but my enemies call me Namor.

00:01:20.275 --> 00:01:23.419
RUTH E. CARTER
We are all trying to make this as accurate

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:26.430
as possible,
but we are creating a subculture.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.344
The Talokanil, they lived underwater
for thousands of years.

00:01:31.414 --> 00:01:36.262
So, we went from historical
reference to imagination.

00:01:36.313 --> 00:01:38.309
LETITIA WRIGHT
It's beautiful to see Ruth really go

00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:40.397
the extra mile and
get that resource,

00:01:40.447 --> 00:01:43.036
get that knowledge
and infuse it into this film.

00:01:44.157 --> 00:01:46.001
LUPITA NYONG'O
Working with Ruth is really fascinating

00:01:46.051 --> 00:01:51.945
because she's the calmest creator I know
and she's so humorous and light as she's

00:01:51.995 --> 00:01:58.346
creating these really intense costumes
that are going to inform cosplay for

00:01:58.396 --> 00:02:00.258
a decade to come
or more, you know?

00:02:00.308 --> 00:02:02.046
RUTH E. CARTER
To come back to Wakanda,

00:02:02.096 --> 00:02:08.007
to be able to present African culture in
a futuristic way that was not colonized,

00:02:08.057 --> 00:02:11.223
is certainly a highlight of my career.

